Public skill event and replay browser verification
Date: 2026-10-20
Command: PLAYWRIGHT_MODULE=/tmp/b4-browser-check/node_modules/playwright python3 scripts/manual/skill_event_browser_check.py
Exit: 0

Chromium opened the live game UI and delivered frozen public `skill_decision`, existing `skill_activation`, and `dying_rescue` events through the same event callback used by WebSocket messages. The desk log showed the accepted/declined reason and public rescue participants/card; skill decisions received a distinct class without exposing model reasoning.

The script also opened `/logs.html` against a temporary `GameLogStore` fixture served by the actual `/api/logs` handlers. Replay rendered the skill decision and dying rescue as distinct timeline rows in sequence. No browser page errors occurred. Data was isolated under a temporary directory.
